\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  The word of God, the most sweet news
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I shall read it everyday
\par I can see the Lord's nature
\par and his holiness in it.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When He called the little children
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 It's with joy He said to them
\par Let these little ones come to me
\par theirs is the heav'nly kingdom
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  He looked at them with compassion
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  and he raised his hands on them
\par and with all His Godly blessings
\par blessed them all and everyone.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Those who were sick amongst them too
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He loved and healed them as well
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 and those who are to be pitied
\par   he called all of them brothers
\par \pard\li225\sl40\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   The no-to-rious criminals too
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  He rescued and welcome them
\par  He forgave them and saved their lives
\par  Come to me all you people.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. He nurtured the sheep the Father
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj gave, and showed the path to heaven
\par  He raised his hands and said to them
\par " Come to me all you people."
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  Here I come kneeling at your feet
\par      Your love has broken my heart,
\par      I shed tears before you, Jesus
\par      feeling relieved in your sight.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

